  topicId: bluecarbon
  title: Blue carbon
  body: Carbon stored by coastal plants such as mangroves and seagrass is called
    blue carbon. A hectare of mangroves can hold up to four times the carbon of most
    tropical forests, much of it in the mud under their roots. Clearing them releases
    it as CO2.
